<section class="fidya-guide three-tool-knowledge" id="fidya-guide" aria-labelledby="fidya-guide-heading">
 <h2 id="fidya-guide-heading">Fidya for missed Ramadan fasts: eligibility, calculation and complete guide</h2>
 <p><strong>Short answer:</strong> A possible Fidya feeding estimate is <strong>eligible days × a locally verified amount per day</strong>, but only <em>after</em> a qualified authority has established that Fidya is the correct treatment for those days. <a href="https://quran.com/2/184" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Quran 2:184</a> refers to compensatory feeding; <a href="https://quran.com/2/185" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Quran 2:185</a> also distinguishes days to make up after illness or travel. This tool cannot decide between them.</p>
